rd MRD while the NIPT base matures at roughly 10% growth. That supports the NIPT-maturing drag. The category also includes organ health, so this is not a pure NIPT figure.","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001604821/000160482126000015/ntra-20260630xex991.htm","date":"2026-08-06","source_name":"Natera 8-K Ex. 99.1 (Q2'26); Q1'26 release https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001604821/000162828026032101/ntra-20260331xex991.htm","source_type":"filing","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"The known list cites total +22% and oncology +57% but not the derived non-oncology y/y of about +10-12% or the sequential dip."},{"label":"1C","direction":"against","claim":"Natera's oncology tests are growing fast and are gaining share of the mix, which gives Illumina volume support.","detail":"Oncology tests processed were about 296.7K in Q2'26 (+57.2% y/y) and 258.9K in Q1'26 (+54.4%). Sequentially that is +14.6% q/q, and clinical MRD units rose 34K q/q, the largest sequential increase to date. Q2 total tests of about 1.04M were up 22.4%, against +18.5% in Q1, so total test growth accelerated. Natera raised FY26 revenue guidance to $2.85-2.91B. This cuts against the claim that NTRA is not seeing MRD become a meaningful share of its mix. Oncology went from about 22% to about 28% of tests in a year. The caveat is that tests are not Gb, as the known list already notes.","url":"https://www.natera.com/company/news/natera-reports-second-quarter-2026-financial-results/","date":"2026-08-06","source_name":"Natera Q2'26 press release","source_type":"filing","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"This quantifies the oncology mix share (22% to 28%) and the Q1'26 oncology figure of 258.9K, which are not in the known list."}],"new_candidates":["Natera 8-K Ex. 99.1 for each quarter from Q1'24 to Q4'25, to build the full non-oncology and oncology table","Natera Q2'26 call transcript on Panorama enhancement, NIPT market growth and sequencing cost per test","Natera 10-Q Q2'2